/// What this build's Leitmotif listens to, for the "What is this?" page.
enum Edition {
    static let name = "Ambit"
    static let leitmotifSource = "Your iPhone's own network counters: how many bytes and packets it sends and receives, about 15 times a second. Never what's in them or who they're to: no content, no names, no VPN."
    static let leitmotifMapping = "Traffic is cut into bursts, and each burst becomes a letter by direction (sent or received) and size (small, medium, large). The last three letters make a word, and each word seeds a short motif of two to four notes, so a habit (streaming, messaging, scrolling) always gets the same tune. Big downloads sing an octave lower; tiny keep-alives are whispered two octaves up. Download rate sets how hard the keys are struck, upload rate how much tape dust rides along."
}
